From 19f6a3239b476baadc4a3235e37ca53829b08009 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: zzl <zzl@google.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 16:39:58 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 5/5] [Model] glm5_next: MTP speculative decoding on the
 unified KV pool

GLM-5.3-Flash ships one MTP layer (checkpoint layer 45). This adds the
draft head and makes the indexer's member state speculative-safe, on top
of the pooled-KDA checkpoint support (#1711, #1811).

- glm5_next/mtp.py: Glm5NextMTP. enorm/hnorm + eh_proj over
  [embed, hidden], one sparse-MLA + MoE block, shared_head norm; embed and
  lm_head shared with the target. Weights load from model.layers.45.
- glm5_next_spec_patch.py: registers glm5_next as an MTP model type and
  points the draft config at Glm5NextMTPModel.
- indexer: the member ring holds kpool + num_spec rows, so a verify window
  can complete a pool from members written up to num_spec positions back;
  it is read from the checkpoint block the read offset selects and written
  to every checkpoint block of the window.
- attention: the draft's MLA skips the all-heads twins; that path
  specializes its trace to the token count, and the draft is traced once
  for all buckets.
- eagle3: never compile or call the draft at one token (size-1 guards
  specialize away the other buckets); accept the pool-key layers the GLM
  unified pool folds into the MLA group.
- scheduler: a decode takes 1 + num_spec tokens of the prefill budget.
- unified_pool: a mamba group only needs a matching page (its block_size
  is the whole context when not in align mode).

Validated (TP8, 16K ctx and 200K production config):
- GSM8K 600: K=1 94.83%, K=3 94.83%, no spec 95.33%.
- Long-context exact recall (3K-13K tokens, 210 questions): K=3 200,
  no spec 197.
- Single-stream decode: K=1 ~1.5x, K=3 1.8-2.3x (117 -> 210-264 tok/s).
  The gain shrinks with concurrency (20K in / 700 out, per chip:
  c1 28.6 -> 62.4, c8 157.9 -> 172.4 tok/s).

